00:57:04,000 --> 00:57:10,000
Sugarcane is a 2024 documentary film, directed by Julian Brave NoiseCat and
Emily Kassie and produced by Emily Kassie and Kellen Quinn.

9
01:04:12,000 --> 01:04:18,000
It follows an investigation into the Canadian Indian residential school system,
igniting a reckoning in the lives of survivors and descendants.

10
01:11:20,000 --> 01:11:26,000
It had its world premiere at the Sundance Film Festival on January 20,
2024 where it won the Grand Jury award for Directing.

11
01:18:28,000 --> 01:18:34,000
It was theatrically released in limited engagements in the United States and Canada  on August 9, 2024, before gradually expanding to other cities
starting August 16, by National Geographic Documentary Films through Variance Films in the United States and Films We Like in Canada.

12
01:25:36,000 --> 01:25:42,000
It received critical acclaim and won the award for Best
Documentary at the National Board of Review.

13
01:32:44,000 --> 01:32:50,000
At the 97th Academy Awards, it was nominated for the
Best Documentary Feature Film award.

14
01:39:52,000 --> 01:39:58,000
The film explores themes of child abuse, somber, bitter, tragic, urgent.
